<article class="env-remark" id="01B0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01B0">Remark <span data-tag="01B0">17.6.4</span>.</a> In Sheaves, Remark <a href="/tag/00AI" data-tag="00AI">6.32.5</a> we showed that $i_*$ as a functor on the categories of sheaves of sets does not have a right adjoint simply because it is not exact. However, it is very close to being true, in fact, the functor $i_*$ is exact on sheaves of pointed sets, sections with support in $Z$ can be defined for sheaves of pointed sets, and $\mathcal{H}_ Z$ makes sense and is a right adjoint to $i_*$. </p>
</article>